BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] System Outage March 21 - Arrêt de service de la grappe Ced
 ar le 21 mars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220321T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220322T000000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-737@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:System Outage March 21\n-------------------------------\nThe C
 edar system will be unavailable starting March 21 for system updates:\nope
 rating system\, filesystem software\, OmniPath drivers\, scheduler softwar
 e.\nJobs submitted with a runtime request that would extend into the downt
 ime will not start before the downtime.\nFor information see: https://docs
 .computecanada.ca/wiki/Cedar Email [email protected] for assistance and/o
 r to report problems.\nArrêt de service de la grappe Cedar le 21 mars\n--
 --------------------------------------------\nLa grappe Cedar ne sera pas 
 disponible à compter du 21 mars alors que nous effectuerons les mises à 
 jour suivantes : système d’exploitation\, logiciel des systèmes de fic
 hiers\, pilotes OmniPath\, ordonnanceur. Les tâches soumises avec une lim
 ite de temps qui chevauche la période d’arrêt ne démarreront pas avan
 t le retour en service.\nPour plus d’information\, lisez : https://docs.
 computecanada.ca/wiki/Cedar Écrivez à [email protected] pour obtenir de
  l’aide ou rapporter un problème.\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view
 _incident?incident=737
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=737
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220328T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220328T110000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-741@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Starting Monday\, March 28th\, 2022\, at 10 am ET\, the Graham
  cluster will be unavailable to all users as we perform regular maintenanc
 e. Running jobs will be terminated. The work will be completed by Tuesday\
 , March 29th\, 2022 at 10 am. During this maintenance window we will be up
 grading the scratch file system.\nPlease watch http://status.computecanada
 .ca for updates on the availability of Graham and all other national syste
 ms.\nWe are upgrading the scratch file system to provide better overall pe
 rformance. The upgrade is not expected to impact any files stored on scrat
 ch\; however\, as with any file system maintenance\, issues could potentia
 lly arise. Therefore\, users are encouraged to copy any critical data stor
 ed on scratch to another filesystem ahead of this maintenance.\nAs a gener
 al reminder: the scratch file system is intended for temporary files\; not
 hing that can’t be recovered or recreated. The scratch file system is no
 t backed up.\nThis outage will impact the cluster\, login nodes\, visualiz
 ation nodes (VDI) as well as data transfer nodes (DTN). There will be no i
 mpact to the Graham cloud.\nStart Time : 10 am ET\, Monday\, March 28\, 20
 22 Anticipated End Time : 10 am ET\, Tuesday\, March 29\, 2022 Users will 
 be notified by email when the cluster is up and running again.\nFor questi
 ons\, or assistance migrating to other national systems\, please email [em
 ail protected] Thank you\, Graham Team\, Compute Canada Federation\n\nhtt
 ps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=741
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=741
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Cedar] External network outage - Panne du réseau externe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20220402T060000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20220402T070000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-746@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:This is a reminder advisory that the planned activity BCNET Co
 re Network Maintenance in Vancouver is to start on Saturday\, April 2\, 20
 22 at 06:00 AM Pacific Time.\nVancouver – VANTX - CR2.VNCV1 vulnerabilit
 y troubleshooting From: 06:00 PT Saturday\, April 2\, 2022 To: 10:00 PT Sa
 turday\, April 2\, 2022 Reason: BCNET Network Engineers together with Juni
 per Advanced TAC will be troubleshooting an existing vulnerability on the 
 CR2.VNCV1 Core Router at the BCNET Vancouver Exchange\, VANTX.\nNo configu
 ration changes to current connections will be done during this maintenance
 .\nEffects: BCNET performed a similar CR2.VNCV1 emergency maintenance on F
 ebruary 26\, 2022.\nWe expect several 20-minute outages to occur during th
 is maintenance window.\nMembers with a connection to only this router will
  experience downtime for all L2 and L3 services (Transit\, IX and ORAN).\n
 Please reply to [email protected] email if you need additional details to
  assess the risk for your organization.\nContact: Please contact the BCNET
  Operations Center at 604-424-0489 option 3 or [email protected] when net
 work problems are experienced outside of a maintenance window.\nPosted By:
  BCNET Network Management Center 604-424-0489 option 3 [email protected]\
 n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=746
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=746
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] (Update) Planned Outage - (Mise-à-jour) Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220502T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220502T130000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-752@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Narval will be unavailable from 9:00 PM EDT on May 2 until 12:
 00 PM EDT on May 3 due to an electrical outage required for Beluga’s ret
 urn to service.\nThis planned outage will only affect Narval’s compute n
 odes .\nAll other services\, including login nodes\, storage\, the Béluga
  cloud and Juno secure cloud will be available.\nAny jobs that have been s
 ubmitted and which have a duration that would extend beyond the start of t
 he outage will not start until service is restored.\nNo action is required
  on your part.\nEn raison d’une coupure électrique nécessaire aux trav
 aux de remise en service de Béluga\, Narval ne sera pas disponible à par
 tir de 21h HAE le 2 mai jusqu’à 12h HAE le 3 mai .\nCette coupure affec
 te uniquement les nœuds de calcul de Narval .\nTous les autres services\,
  incluant les nœuds de tête\, le stockage\, le nuage Béluga\, ainsi que
  le nuage sécurisé Juno resteront accessibles.\nLes tâches qui auraient
  été soumises et dont l’exécution se prolongerait au-delà de l’arr
 êt ne démarreront qu'une fois le service rétabli.\nAucune action n’es
 t requise de votre part .\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?i
 ncident=752
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=752
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220505T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220505T080000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-755@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:On Thursday May 5th\, 2022\, starting from 7:00 am EDT\, an up
 grade of the scheduler of the Niagara\, Mist\, and Rouge clusters will be 
 applied.\nThis requires the scheduler to be down for about 5-6 hours\, and
  all compute and login nodes to be rebooted.\nJobs cannot be submitted dur
 ing this maintenance\, but jobs submitted beforehand will remain in the qu
 eue.  For most of the time\, the login nodes of the clusters will be avai
 lable so that users may access their files on the home\, scratch\, and pro
 ject file systems.\n-- Ce jeudi 5 mai 2022 à partir de 07h00 Heure Avanc
 ée de l'Est aura lieu une mise à jour de l'ordonnanceur pour les grappes
  Niagara\, MIST et Rouge. L'ordonnanceur sera hors service pour une durée
  de 5-6 heures\, et tous les noeuds de connexion et de calcul seront redé
 marrés.\nPendant cette maintenance\, aucune tâche ne pourra être exécu
 tée\, mais les tâches soumises précédemment seront maintenues dans la 
 file d'attente. Les noeuds de connexion seront disponibles aux usagers la 
 plupart du temps\, leur permettant d'accéder aux fichiers se trouvant dan
 s les espaces 'home'\, 'scratch' et 'project'.\n\nhttps://status.alliancec
 an.ca/view_incident?incident=755
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=755
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[DRAC] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20220525T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20220525T100000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-761@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:Starting Wednesday\, May 25th\, 2022\, at 9 am ET\, the Graham
  cluster will be unavailable to all users as we perform an upgrade of the 
 project file system. All running jobs will be terminated but queued jobs w
 ill remain. Queued jobs that would extend past the beginning of the outage
  will not be allowed to launch until after the maintenance.  The work wil
 l be completed by Thursday\, May 26th\, 2022 at 10 am.\nAt this time we wi
 ll also reduce the maximum job duration to 7 days on Graham. This is the s
 ame scheduler configuration as the Narval and Beluga clusters. Cedar will 
 continue to accept jobs with a duration of more than 7 days.\nPlease watch
  https://status.computecanada.ca for updates on the availability of Graham
  and all other national systems.\nWe are upgrading the project file system
  to provide better overall performance. The upgrade is not expected to cau
 se data loss\; however\, as with any file system maintenance\, issues coul
 d potentially arise. Should issues arise\, we could recover files from the
  daily backups.\nThis outage will impact the cluster\, login nodes\, visua
 lization nodes (VDI) as well as data transfer nodes (DTN). There will be n
 o impact to the Graham cloud.\nStart Time: 9 am ET\, Wednesday\, May 25\, 
 2022 Anticipated End Time: 10 am ET\, Thursday\, May 26\, 2022 Users will 
 be notified by email when the cluster is up and running again.\nFor questi
 ons\, or assistance migrating to other national systems\, please email [em
 ail protected]\n\nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=76
 1
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=761
END:VEVENT
